{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-progress bias, routes every obstacle observation through a dedicated recovery state, uses backward motion only as a one-shot response to front obstacles, prefers directed turns away from side obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately when path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use one policy automaton to map sensed conditions to exactly one allowed action per decision state",
    "Use dedicated one-shot recovery states for obstacle handling",
    "Bias clear operation toward move_forward and use random_walk only as a secondary exploration mode",
    "Keep action states robust to open-loop pulse semantics by self-looping on path_clear and only letting obstacle events preempt when safety-critical"
  ],
